<title>SPAIN: DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>DIVING-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SEVILLE, Spain 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diving results from the</p>
<p>seventh day of the European championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Men's three-metre synchronised diving final. (Five dives</p>
<p>each)</p>
<p>1. Germany (Holgar Schlepps, Alexander Mesch) 284.34 points</p>
<p>2. Spain (Jose Luis Hidalgo, Ruben Santos) 283.92</p>
<p>3. Italy (Nicola Marconi, Ruben Santos) 277.38</p>
<p>4. Britain (Antonio Ali, Mark Shipman) 274.71</p>
<p>5. Ukraine (Valery Statsenko, Alexei Ilyin) 262.23</p>
<p>6. France (Gilles Emptoz-Lacote, Frederic Pierre) 252.27</p>
<p>Women's ten-metre synchronised diving final (Five dives</p>
<p>each)</p>
<p>1. Germany (Ute Wetzig, Anke Piper) 269.76 points</p>
<p>2. France (Odile Arboles-Souchon, Julie Danaux) 240.54</p>
<p>3. Austria (Marion Reiff, Anja Richter) 215.67</p>
<p>4. Russia (Evgenia Olshevskaya, Olga Khristoforova) 208.98</p>
<p>5. Britain (Hayley Allen, Lesley Ward) 201.21</p>
</text>
